WEBVTT

00:50.091 --> 00:52.844
ALL CHARACTERS, LOCATIONS,
ORGANIZATIONS, RELIGIONS,

00:52.927 --> 00:55.764
EVENTS, AND OCCUPATIONS
IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:56.431 --> 00:58.183
What is it? What happened?

00:59.142 --> 01:01.061
- Did someone die?
- Dead bodies?

01:01.144 --> 01:03.772
- What is it?
- Is it a murder case?

01:03.855 --> 01:06.191
Why won't they tell us?

01:20.413 --> 01:25.335
…or command locusts to devour the land
or send a plague among my people.

01:25.418 --> 01:27.712
If my people, who are called by my name,

01:27.796 --> 01:31.966
will humble themselves
and pray and seek my face

01:32.050 --> 01:34.219
and turn from their wicked ways,

01:34.302 --> 01:36.429
then I will hear from heaven,

01:36.513 --> 01:40.934
and I will forgive their sin
and will heal their land.

01:41.893 --> 01:44.062
Now my eyes will be open

01:44.145 --> 01:47.106
and my ears will be attentive
to the prayers offered in this place.

01:47.732 --> 01:51.903
I have chosen and consecrated this temple…

02:07.293 --> 02:09.170
One of the homeless people had pneumonia,

02:09.254 --> 02:10.588
so they gave him medicine.

02:11.214 --> 02:13.925
It was donated, so they didn't know
about the side effects.

02:38.032 --> 02:40.451
Reports of a disease
that causes the infected

02:40.535 --> 02:43.746
to bite people and suck their blood
are coming from all over the world.

02:43.830 --> 02:48.001
The public health authorities made clear
that it hasn't been confirmed yet,

02:48.084 --> 02:51.004
but similar cases are also occurring
in Korea.

02:51.087 --> 02:54.799
In a shelter for the homeless in Seyang,
around ten homeless individuals

02:54.883 --> 02:57.468
who were staying there were killed.

02:58.428 --> 03:01.514
The authorities stated
that there was a random fight

03:01.598 --> 03:04.809
among the homeless at the shelter,
which caused casualties,

03:04.893 --> 03:06.686
so there may be possible sanitary…

03:06.769 --> 03:08.646
SUSPECTED TO BE AN INFECTIOUS DISEASE

03:08.730 --> 03:10.273
You're eating plants again?

03:11.900 --> 03:13.985
Sae-bom, are you okay?

03:14.569 --> 03:17.488
Yes, I got tested and got myself together.

03:20.825 --> 03:22.619
Just what in the world is going on?

03:24.412 --> 03:26.205
We stopped all the drills.

03:26.289 --> 03:29.500
They shut down the training area
where Lee Jong-tae caused a scene.

03:33.379 --> 03:35.632
He's that man from before, right?

03:36.799 --> 03:38.426
Yes, he is.

03:38.509 --> 03:39.928
He really does have some power.

03:43.473 --> 03:45.600
What if something really bad happens?

03:46.935 --> 03:49.562
If people suddenly start
to go mad like that…

03:50.647 --> 03:52.565
There is a cure for this, right?

03:53.816 --> 03:54.984
I don't know.

03:55.902 --> 03:57.987
It looks like they're
trying their best, but…

04:02.325 --> 04:04.077
I got a call from a journalist.

04:04.994 --> 04:08.498
He said he'll pay me
if I tell him what happened here.

04:08.581 --> 04:09.582
Me too.

04:10.250 --> 04:13.169
Looks like he contacted
everyone on our team.

04:13.920 --> 04:16.339
Hey, don't contact people like him.

04:17.131 --> 04:18.883
We even signed a confidentiality oath.

04:20.176 --> 04:21.010
Right.

04:23.596 --> 04:25.682
- Are you returning to work now?
- No.

04:26.307 --> 04:28.434
I received paid leave for six months.

04:28.518 --> 04:30.353
I stopped by to say hi today

04:30.436 --> 04:32.230
after sending my stuff to my new house.

04:32.313 --> 04:34.190
Are you leaving the public official dorm?

04:34.274 --> 04:36.109
You worked so hard to decorate it.

04:36.192 --> 04:37.402
It's okay.

04:38.444 --> 04:40.488
I got a house.

04:42.365 --> 04:43.616
An apartment.

04:45.785 --> 04:47.245
- With a loan?
- No.

04:47.328 --> 04:49.497
Remember when we talked about
additional points?

04:49.580 --> 04:50.915
The special provision.

04:50.999 --> 04:53.459
I do. Work evaluation, arrest records…

04:53.543 --> 04:57.338
I got the highest points,
but I still lacked points for that.

04:57.422 --> 05:01.134
So I decided to get points
for newlyweds too.

05:03.219 --> 05:09.142
You mean… You're going to get married
because you need more points?

05:09.225 --> 05:10.226
Yes.

05:11.602 --> 05:12.979
Who are you going to marry?

05:13.062 --> 05:15.815
There's this guy who asked me out
when we were young.

05:15.898 --> 05:17.400
I rejected him at the time.

05:17.483 --> 05:21.195
But I asked him
if he still has feelings for me.

05:21.779 --> 05:24.449
It's not because
I don't take you seriously.

05:25.325 --> 05:26.242
I…

05:28.494 --> 05:30.913
I always dreamed
of living in my own house.

05:32.248 --> 05:33.333
That's why.

05:38.671 --> 05:40.798
These are for the clothes we burned.

05:42.341 --> 05:43.676
Thank you.

05:43.760 --> 05:45.762
I feel like I've gotten closer to you.

05:50.391 --> 05:52.143
She's cold.

05:56.647 --> 05:59.150
- Do you need more points?
- That's true, but…

06:04.280 --> 06:07.200
I asked you
because I have feelings for you.

06:07.283 --> 06:10.036
You're not so bad on the eyes,
and you are resourceful.

06:10.828 --> 06:13.164
Hey, I'm a lot better than you think.

06:13.247 --> 06:16.375
Being two years behind? That's nothing.
Plus, it's a newly built apartment.

06:16.459 --> 06:18.169
If you miss this,
you'll regret it forever.

06:21.547 --> 06:26.302
Hey! You can't find
another friend like me.

06:29.180 --> 06:30.223
Okay, sure.

06:38.648 --> 06:39.774
I'm asking you…

06:40.691 --> 06:42.026
to marry me.

06:42.819 --> 06:44.028
I know what you mean.

06:44.862 --> 06:45.780
I'm saying yes.

06:47.156 --> 06:48.074
He said yes.

06:52.870 --> 06:54.330
He said yes.

06:56.415 --> 06:58.501
Oh… Congratulations.

06:59.627 --> 07:00.670
Oh, well…

07:01.921 --> 07:04.006
- When are you moving in?
- Today.

07:12.598 --> 07:15.726
This is the scratch Lee Jong-tae made,
and it's not healing that well.

07:17.145 --> 07:18.438
It didn't get worse, though?

07:19.272 --> 07:21.357
No. They want to draw
my blood every two weeks.

07:22.191 --> 07:23.025
I see.

07:30.408 --> 07:31.284
Are you okay?

07:33.286 --> 07:34.162
What?

07:34.871 --> 07:36.914
Yes, I'm okay.

07:41.961 --> 07:45.756
(I AM) THE LIFESAVER

07:47.049 --> 07:48.176
Aren't you taking that?

07:49.427 --> 07:50.344
I will.

07:51.179 --> 07:52.346
Hang on.

08:00.813 --> 08:02.273
I'm going to go home now.

08:02.356 --> 08:05.276
I'll organize your stuff when they arrive.
You take your time.

08:05.359 --> 08:06.819
- Okay.
- Okay.

08:08.571 --> 08:10.990
You're putting in so much effort.

08:21.918 --> 08:25.421
DEDICATED TO THE SECURITY OF THE HOMELAND

08:39.560 --> 08:42.522
Corporal, have you thought about it?

08:42.605 --> 08:44.065
How much can you pay me?

08:45.608 --> 08:48.110
I talked to the director,

08:48.194 --> 08:49.779
and if there is internal footage

08:49.862 --> 08:51.280
and if we get an exclusive,

08:51.364 --> 08:54.158
I think we can do our best
to give you the amount you ask for.

08:56.285 --> 08:59.705
Why don't you get in?
Let's talk comfortably.

09:30.528 --> 09:32.029
Hang in there, okay?

09:33.114 --> 09:34.365
It's okay.

09:49.630 --> 09:51.716
Seung-young, what are you doing?

10:02.977 --> 10:03.894
Here.

10:06.772 --> 10:07.607
Thank you.

10:07.690 --> 10:10.151
How can you remember
a picture from 12 years ago?

10:10.234 --> 10:11.944
I almost got killed back then.

10:12.028 --> 10:13.696
Anyway, congratulations. You did it.

10:13.779 --> 10:15.948
Though I didn't expect it
to work out like this.

10:23.914 --> 10:24.749
Move!

10:24.832 --> 10:27.251
- Why? What is it?
- My gift for you.

10:27.335 --> 10:28.169
Come on.

10:28.252 --> 10:30.254
My wife started working a side job.

10:31.047 --> 10:34.175
Don't worry. She's all better now,
completely healthy.

10:34.258 --> 10:35.509
We also do delivery.

10:35.593 --> 10:38.137
Hand them around the apartment
and spread the word about our shop.

10:38.220 --> 10:40.598
You should be helping your wife,
not making things hard for her.

10:40.681 --> 10:44.727
About the info
on Han Tae-seok like you asked…

10:44.810 --> 10:46.896
I will do my best. What is it?

10:47.647 --> 10:49.398
He specializes in infectious diseases.

10:49.482 --> 10:51.734
Some of the military academy
students are sent

10:51.817 --> 10:54.028
to a medical school
as commissioned education.

10:54.111 --> 10:57.698
He became a doctor through that, served
as a medic, and finished his service.

10:57.782 --> 11:00.242
After that, he worked
at a pharmaceutical company.

11:00.326 --> 11:03.537
He was the Team Leader
of Competitiveness Reinforcement.

11:04.121 --> 11:04.997
And…

11:10.378 --> 11:12.797
This was taken during his trial
for assaulting the CEO

11:12.880 --> 11:14.465
of the pharmaceutical company.

11:15.466 --> 11:17.385
He didn't look like the type to do that.

11:17.885 --> 11:20.930
Those who look well-mannered
are scarier when they lose it.

11:22.056 --> 11:23.891
Anyway, he was suddenly found innocent,

11:23.974 --> 11:25.476
and he went back to the military.

11:25.559 --> 11:27.645
As a dispatch to the CDSCHQ.

11:28.938 --> 11:29.814
That's weird.

11:31.065 --> 11:33.609
Anyway, try not to get involved in this.

11:33.692 --> 11:36.237
You'll just get yourself in trouble
by meddling in it.

11:36.320 --> 11:37.321
Okay.

11:37.405 --> 11:38.614
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

11:38.697 --> 11:41.075
And if you need more rice cakes,
tell me, okay?

11:41.158 --> 11:42.701
- Okay.
- Okay, bye.

11:54.213 --> 11:56.090
I don't want to get involved either,

11:57.049 --> 11:58.551
but I think that'll be hard.

12:11.730 --> 12:17.653
SEYANG FOREST LE CIEL
WELCOME, NEW RESIDENTS

12:30.458 --> 12:34.086
That trainee I gave first aid to.

12:35.045 --> 12:38.007
- He kept coming to mind.
- What about him?

12:40.384 --> 12:43.888
He's in bad condition,
just like Lee Jong-tae.

12:45.556 --> 12:47.308
Even his family can't visit him.

12:48.392 --> 12:51.020
I asked the guys who were
dispatched to the CDSCHQ,

12:52.813 --> 12:56.984
and they said once you go in there,
you can't come out alive.

12:59.320 --> 13:00.529
But I came out alive.

13:01.197 --> 13:02.031
Right.

13:02.781 --> 13:05.576
Only you did.

13:14.251 --> 13:16.128
Is this really okay?

13:16.962 --> 13:18.923
What if everyone is dying in there?

13:22.968 --> 13:26.430
It's so difficult to be happy.

13:41.237 --> 13:42.738
You scared me!

13:43.364 --> 13:45.699
Sorry. You need to be careful.

13:45.783 --> 13:47.451
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

13:52.331 --> 13:53.874
That scared me.

14:27.575 --> 14:29.994
I'm going to the fifth floor. Thank you.

14:37.209 --> 14:39.211
Please wear a mask indoors.

14:41.171 --> 14:43.215
Okay, I'm sorry.

14:50.764 --> 14:52.016
That hoodie…

14:53.517 --> 14:55.185
Where did you buy that?

14:55.269 --> 14:57.146
It looks genuine, not custom-made.

14:59.023 --> 15:00.024
I'm in the SOU.

15:00.983 --> 15:03.819
The real SOU?

15:03.903 --> 15:06.280
You're a tactical agent
who fights terrorist attacks?

15:06.363 --> 15:07.489
Yes.

15:07.573 --> 15:11.076
Can you please get me an SOU T-shirt?

15:11.702 --> 15:14.830
The one that has SOU
printed in the front and back.

15:14.914 --> 15:15.956
Large-sized.

15:20.085 --> 15:22.880
I'll look into it. Large, you said?

15:22.963 --> 15:27.051
Yes, please do. I'm on the 15th floor.

15:32.932 --> 15:34.433
He's eccentric.

15:55.621 --> 15:56.830
You're early.

15:56.914 --> 15:58.874
We should celebrate with delivery food.

15:58.958 --> 16:02.294
I knew you'd say that, so I searched
for good restaurants already.

16:02.378 --> 16:03.921
Hey, you had this picture?

16:04.672 --> 16:07.007
Jung-kook had the file.

16:08.175 --> 16:09.218
So I had it developed.

16:10.010 --> 16:11.136
Don't you like it?

16:11.220 --> 16:12.513
Well…

16:13.013 --> 16:16.350
But this situation
wasn't that joyful for you at the time.

16:16.433 --> 16:17.476
Do you like it?

16:20.229 --> 16:22.690
Hey! Stand straight.

16:22.773 --> 16:25.067
Okay, here we go! One, two, three!

16:26.694 --> 16:29.279
When life is hard, look at this,
and do your best in life.

16:34.702 --> 16:35.786
There.

16:38.497 --> 16:41.500
Well, you said the district office
can come and check

16:41.583 --> 16:43.168
if we really are married.

16:43.752 --> 16:46.755
This would show why we got married.

16:46.839 --> 16:48.590
It's a very powerful motive.

16:48.674 --> 16:51.719
Right. It looks like
there's a deep story behind us.

16:59.018 --> 17:00.811
It's nice I'm cuffed.

17:00.894 --> 17:03.731
When would I ever experience
getting cuffed again?

17:05.774 --> 17:07.317
Are you passing around rice cakes?

17:07.818 --> 17:10.821
It's Jung-kook's side job.
He wants me to advertise them.

17:10.904 --> 17:11.780
Okay.

17:12.740 --> 17:14.825
- I'll be back soon--
- No, I'll do it.

17:15.409 --> 17:16.744
You get the house organized

17:16.827 --> 17:19.288
and order black bean noodles.
I want a double portion.

17:19.872 --> 17:20.706
Okay.

17:21.457 --> 17:23.375
- Hey, be careful.
- Okay.

17:44.813 --> 17:45.981
Who is it?

17:46.732 --> 17:48.984
I moved in next door.
Aren't the grown-ups home?

18:01.121 --> 18:02.039
Hi.

18:04.917 --> 18:06.919
Thank you, I will enjoy it.

18:09.755 --> 18:10.714
Bye.

18:29.274 --> 18:30.109
What?

18:41.870 --> 18:42.830
It won't open.

18:44.498 --> 18:46.792
The lower floors are public rentals,

18:46.875 --> 18:48.710
and the upper ones are regular apartments.

18:48.794 --> 18:51.505
They blocked it to stop people downstairs
from coming up.

18:51.588 --> 18:53.132
You know all kinds of things.

18:53.215 --> 18:56.426
I know everything.
Kids call us beggars at school.

19:00.013 --> 19:02.808
- How do they come down from upstairs?
- By taking the elevator.

19:10.149 --> 19:12.234
- Are you going downstairs?
- Yes.

19:13.652 --> 19:14.778
One apartment is empty,

19:14.862 --> 19:16.905
and a lady lives alone
in the other apartment,

19:16.989 --> 19:18.615
but she didn't come home yesterday.

19:19.449 --> 19:20.868
You really know everything.

19:38.302 --> 19:39.887
That's better.

19:44.516 --> 19:45.601
Jeez.

19:46.685 --> 19:48.270
Is it okay to do this?

19:48.353 --> 19:51.815
Yes. Blocking an emergency exit
is a violation of the Fire Prevention Act.

19:51.899 --> 19:53.942
If they complain, we can report them.

19:54.818 --> 19:56.195
I see.

19:56.278 --> 19:57.779
Okay then, see you later.

20:14.504 --> 20:16.632
The insurance companies
always say it's 50-50.

20:16.715 --> 20:19.551
Keeping a safe distance,
obligation to look forward. Right?

20:19.635 --> 20:22.429
Don't mind what those parrots
are squawking about.

20:22.512 --> 20:24.640
I saw the footage. And 90-10 is possible.

20:25.265 --> 20:28.393
I'm from Unit 501.
I moved in today, so I brought rice cakes.

20:29.269 --> 20:30.354
Please excuse me.

20:37.861 --> 20:40.489
We're neighbors, so
I'll provide legal counseling for free.

20:40.572 --> 20:42.699
So come anytime and consult me.

20:43.700 --> 20:45.410
Yes, that's what you should do.

20:47.454 --> 20:48.288
SPECIALIZES IN DIVORCE AND CAR ACCIDENTS

20:50.207 --> 20:53.669
"Lawyer Kook Hae-seong,
who appears like a comet in hard times."

20:53.752 --> 20:55.796
Those are separate. Yes.

20:55.879 --> 20:56.713
1:1 COUNSELING CHAT
WITH LAWYER KOOK HAE-SEONG

20:56.797 --> 20:58.715
Yes, you can check and call me again.

21:00.592 --> 21:02.052
That's a separate matter.

21:02.135 --> 21:02.970
IT'S A HIT-AND-RUN
IT'S NOT ME, MY FRIEND DID IT

21:03.053 --> 21:04.221
Yes.

21:04.304 --> 21:05.889
Of course. Call me anytime.

21:05.973 --> 21:08.183
Okay, thank you.

21:08.267 --> 21:10.102
ARE YOU GOING TO TURN YOURSELF IN?

21:10.686 --> 21:12.104
- Who was it?
- Downstairs.

21:13.897 --> 21:14.940
She just moved in.

21:16.149 --> 21:19.027
But you're throwing away food?

21:21.113 --> 21:22.906
You've worked as a lawyer's secretary.

21:22.990 --> 21:25.033
How can you be so gullible?

21:25.117 --> 21:27.369
You shouldn't eat food
a stranger gives you.

21:28.495 --> 21:32.833
So the woman downstairs
gave us poisoned rice cake to kill us?

21:33.750 --> 21:37.087
Honey, you have a psychological problem.

21:37.170 --> 21:40.299
So-yoon, I was once a public defender.

21:40.382 --> 21:43.635
I learned about
people's evil intentions quite early.

21:44.303 --> 21:45.137
Fine.

21:45.220 --> 21:48.056
Then as a public defender,
please go consult them.

21:48.140 --> 21:50.267
That one really needs
an attorney right now.

21:51.560 --> 21:52.728
Good grief.

21:58.108 --> 21:59.943
Of course you'll get caught, you fool.

22:00.652 --> 22:03.280
I'm sure the cops are
on their way to your house now.

22:03.363 --> 22:06.575
WILL I GET CAUGHT IF
I DON'T TURN MYSELF IN?

22:09.119 --> 22:11.413
FIRST, I MUST FIND OUT
IF THE ACCIDENT WAS REPORTED

22:11.496 --> 22:13.582
CAN I GET IN TOUCH WITH YOUR FRIEND?

22:51.203 --> 22:52.370
Who are you?

22:54.706 --> 22:55.707
Hi.

22:55.791 --> 22:59.002
I moved in downstairs.
Here's rice cake for you.

23:00.837 --> 23:02.964
I don't like food made from flour.

23:04.341 --> 23:06.843
But this is "rice" cake.

23:16.478 --> 23:17.938
Nice to meet you too.

23:21.149 --> 23:22.067
Honey.

23:24.653 --> 23:25.737
Honey.

23:26.696 --> 23:27.531
Hey.

23:28.532 --> 23:29.533
Hey. You're home.

23:30.534 --> 23:32.452
Why didn't you answer the door?

23:32.536 --> 23:34.579
I was washing my hair.

23:34.663 --> 23:37.666
Why did you suddenly
press the doorbell, though?

23:37.749 --> 23:41.086
I didn't press it.
Someone came from downstairs.

23:44.172 --> 23:47.592
The apartment is tiny,
and the security is awful.

23:48.260 --> 23:50.262
Hey, Min-ji, wash your hands first.

23:50.345 --> 23:53.014
You should wash your hands
when you come home. 20 seconds.

23:59.479 --> 24:01.481
Are you taking your meds? Hang on.

24:08.280 --> 24:10.198
Here's some water.

24:11.783 --> 24:13.743
I got five complaints today.

24:15.328 --> 24:18.915
Why do they ask for so much
over a few shots of fillers?

24:20.333 --> 24:23.503
This is why I didn't want to do
a franchise dermatology clinic.

24:23.587 --> 24:24.713
I'm sorry.

24:24.796 --> 24:27.507
You're doing bothersome work
because of me.

24:28.550 --> 24:33.096
I will make you an awesome glass
of nice, cold tangerine highball.

24:34.472 --> 24:36.516
What is this?
Your legs are as hard as rocks.

24:36.600 --> 24:39.477
I must relieve them all today.

24:41.605 --> 24:44.065
Shall I make you
a tangerine highball first?

24:44.149 --> 24:45.025
Madam.

24:46.651 --> 24:48.278
You're being a good boy today.

25:20.477 --> 25:22.437
COLLECT THE COUPONS

25:22.520 --> 25:25.565
Let's eat 20 dishes
and get a small sweet and sour pork.

25:25.649 --> 25:26.566
Okay.

25:31.404 --> 25:32.239
And this.

25:33.698 --> 25:34.950
What is this?

25:35.033 --> 25:37.369
A contract for joint ownership
when it's switched

25:37.452 --> 25:39.204
to a regular apartment in ten years.

25:40.747 --> 25:43.625
Six to four is okay, right?
Because my points are higher.

25:43.708 --> 25:46.211
Of course. You even saved my life.

25:46.294 --> 25:47.796
- Right?
- Yes.

25:49.714 --> 25:51.508
I wanted to have herringbone flooring,

25:52.175 --> 25:54.511
but it's new flooring,
so I can't rip it out.

25:55.053 --> 25:57.472
Still, this is neat.

26:02.227 --> 26:03.436
I can't believe this.

26:04.980 --> 26:06.064
I have a house now.

26:10.735 --> 26:16.074
White or beige curtains
would be nice and natural, right?

26:16.658 --> 26:17.492
Yes.

26:17.575 --> 26:19.494
Should we install blinds for the veranda?

26:21.037 --> 26:22.414
The lighting seems just fine.

26:22.998 --> 26:25.250
Still, I might buy
a few lighting fixtures.

26:28.378 --> 26:30.338
We'll need
some gym equipment for this room.

26:30.422 --> 26:31.840
Nice.

26:31.923 --> 26:35.135
I prefer stainless steel countertops.

26:37.053 --> 26:38.805
But all this is brand new.

26:39.723 --> 26:41.683
Let's use it for now and replace it later.

26:42.517 --> 26:45.437
Should we replace only
the sink and bathroom faucets?

26:45.520 --> 26:46.354
Sure.

26:47.147 --> 26:48.732
I'll need to make a lot of money.

26:49.566 --> 26:51.860
But it's nice.
It's worth earning money for.

26:51.943 --> 26:53.820
I'll work hard too.

26:55.447 --> 26:56.489
Let's do this.

27:10.086 --> 27:13.423
The District Office can come
for an inspection, so…

27:14.758 --> 27:17.552
- Shall we change it? Or move it?
- No, you did a great job.

27:18.553 --> 27:20.472
We must be meticulous until the very end.

27:22.807 --> 27:23.975
Right.

27:27.812 --> 27:30.732
When I was young, we had a house.

27:33.610 --> 27:37.405
But something went wrong
and we kept moving to smaller houses,

27:37.489 --> 27:39.699
and in the end,
we lived in a semi-basement.

27:41.451 --> 27:43.036
It only had one room.

27:43.870 --> 27:45.997
- Back in high school?
- Yes.

27:47.248 --> 27:49.250
I could wander around outside
during the day,

27:49.334 --> 27:50.668
but I had to sleep at night,

27:50.752 --> 27:53.963
so I went home as late as possible.

27:55.590 --> 27:59.719
We crammed ourselves
into that small room to sleep.

28:06.142 --> 28:09.145
My mom and dad
were always yelling and fighting…

28:11.606 --> 28:13.608
If I just couldn't stand it anymore,

28:14.526 --> 28:16.820
I got my dad's car key and came outside.

28:18.405 --> 28:19.697
I can't take this!

28:20.365 --> 28:22.283
You get paid peanuts, and…

28:43.596 --> 28:45.682
I always wanted to have my own space.

28:48.560 --> 28:50.103
My own space, just for me.

28:56.317 --> 28:58.111
And I finally made it,

29:01.448 --> 29:04.117
so the Earth
shouldn't meet its end just yet.

29:48.578 --> 29:49.746
Good night.

30:27.492 --> 30:29.452
You will end up like me too.

30:43.967 --> 30:44.884
What is it?

30:48.930 --> 30:52.016
What are they doing
in the middle of the night?

30:53.643 --> 30:55.645
Do you want me to go talk to them?

30:57.981 --> 30:58.815
No…

31:00.191 --> 31:01.734
I was just startled, that's all.

31:35.894 --> 31:36.769
Hello?

31:43.318 --> 31:44.319
You mean now?

32:03.504 --> 32:05.506
- Who was it?
- What?

32:06.883 --> 32:09.969
It's a guy I know.
It's because of the investigation.

32:10.053 --> 32:11.971
Get some more sleep. You're on leave.

32:17.936 --> 32:20.855
Why are you collecting her blood?
She's already worn out.

32:20.939 --> 32:22.065
We won't take that much.

32:22.148 --> 32:24.859
You got married thanks to me,
so don't be so mean.

32:26.152 --> 32:28.905
Thanks to you? This was all me.

32:28.988 --> 32:31.157
If I didn't help her
with additional points,

32:31.240 --> 32:33.534
Ms. Yoon Sae-bom
wouldn't have asked you to marry her.

32:39.582 --> 32:42.335
By the way, you come into
someone else's apartment so easily.

32:42.835 --> 32:45.046
Did you see the news about
the homeless shelter?

32:45.129 --> 32:46.005
I did.

32:46.089 --> 32:48.591
The article about Next
being given to the homeless there

32:48.675 --> 32:49.884
will be released today.

32:49.968 --> 32:52.261
Due to concerns about
possible side effects,

32:52.345 --> 32:54.555
the drugs in the market
will be all collected,

32:54.639 --> 32:56.933
and those who sold them illegally
will be punished.

32:57.016 --> 32:58.768
That's the government's conclusion.

32:58.851 --> 33:01.020
But why are you telling me that?

33:03.022 --> 33:05.692
Because we're going to
investigate together.

33:06.693 --> 33:09.362
I sent the document
asking for cooperation to your station.

33:09.445 --> 33:11.531
Well, I'm a bit busy.

33:15.118 --> 33:16.494
As you can see, I…

33:17.161 --> 33:18.413
CHIEF

33:26.295 --> 33:27.422
Yes, Chief.

33:28.339 --> 33:29.173
Okay.

33:32.552 --> 33:34.554
Do I have to do this?

33:37.640 --> 33:40.268
Of course, I should do it. Who else would?

33:53.114 --> 33:53.990
So…

33:55.992 --> 33:57.160
What should I start with?

33:58.661 --> 34:01.122
This is Lee Jong-tae's phone.
It's been unlocked.

34:01.956 --> 34:04.542
Meet the dealer as Lee Jong-tae
and make the arrest.

34:05.209 --> 34:07.211
Is he cooperating
with the investigation too?

34:09.380 --> 34:10.548
Something like that.

34:21.100 --> 34:22.185
But do you know

34:22.727 --> 34:25.813
what the most difficult part
of narcotics investigation is?

34:25.897 --> 34:29.192
These jerks are always
full of suspicion and greed.

34:29.275 --> 34:31.861
We can't even meet them
if we don't pay half in advance.

34:31.944 --> 34:33.571
But the police don't have money.

34:33.654 --> 34:37.116
I'm not saying that I don't want to help,
it's just the investigation can't…

34:38.493 --> 34:40.078
Use it for the investigation.

34:40.161 --> 34:43.081
Make expense reports,
and return the remaining amount.

34:45.124 --> 34:47.335
I heard you worked
at a pharmaceutical company.

34:47.418 --> 34:49.462
That you were in some
competitiveness team.

34:49.545 --> 34:51.464
Competitiveness Reinforcement Team.

34:51.547 --> 34:53.466
It's where we steal
other companies' drugs.

34:53.549 --> 34:57.678
I may not be good at making things,
but I am good at stealing.

34:58.513 --> 34:59.889
And beating people up?

35:01.766 --> 35:03.476
Call me when you arrest the dealer.

35:03.559 --> 35:05.269
I will participate as an observer.

35:07.939 --> 35:09.774
By the way, how much is the amount?

35:09.857 --> 35:12.652
You're not going to say that
the amount is wrong later, right?

35:14.570 --> 35:15.696
Corporal Jung Yi-hyun.

35:17.573 --> 35:19.867
I heard your nickname is
"Great Detective."

35:21.202 --> 35:23.079
Because you always logically infer cases.

35:25.081 --> 35:28.126
They call it "reckless"
or "hoping for good luck."

35:28.209 --> 35:31.921
They say the way I think is weird,
but I somehow get things right.

35:32.880 --> 35:35.967
There's a bias that athletes are dumb.

35:36.759 --> 35:40.721
You must show that you both have
a good brain and good physique.

35:48.604 --> 35:49.981
I seriously hate him.

36:00.950 --> 36:02.451
MS. KIM BOK-NAM

36:09.834 --> 36:10.877
Hey, Mom, what is it?

36:10.960 --> 36:13.504
I heard you moved into
an apartment yesterday.

36:13.588 --> 36:15.339
And you didn't even call me.

36:15.882 --> 36:19.677
Come on. Do I have to hear
about you from Yi-hyun?

36:19.760 --> 36:21.429
Mom, I'm tired.

36:22.305 --> 36:24.974
I got tested for an infectious disease.

36:25.057 --> 36:27.602
I got tested for COVID-19
more than five times.

36:27.685 --> 36:30.438
No, not that. It was for
that infectious disease

36:30.521 --> 36:33.482
- that makes people bite other people.
- You mean Mad Human Disease?

36:33.566 --> 36:35.193
It has a name?

36:35.276 --> 36:38.237
Yes, they say it's similar to rabies
and makes people go mad.

36:38.321 --> 36:40.323
I heard humans can catch rabies too.

36:40.406 --> 36:42.158
My goodness.

36:42.241 --> 36:45.411
So dog owners are in a frenzy right now.

36:45.494 --> 36:47.538
Yes, anyway, it was for that.

36:48.164 --> 36:49.707
I got tested for Mad Human Disease

36:49.790 --> 36:52.126
and I'm now in self-quarantine
at my apartment.

36:52.210 --> 36:55.296
I even had a dream
about biting people last night.

36:55.379 --> 36:56.547
Really?

36:57.632 --> 36:59.842
What about Yi-hyun?
Is he okay with living with you?

37:01.219 --> 37:04.555
Of course. We really do love each other.

37:06.098 --> 37:09.727
I'll recover soon and call you
when our wedding date is set.

37:12.521 --> 37:14.440
I'm starting to cough now. I should go.

37:44.845 --> 37:46.389
I need to go buy groceries.

37:59.402 --> 38:02.989
GYM REGISTRATION PROCESS: RESIDENTS

38:03.072 --> 38:05.199
WEEKDAYS: 6:00 TO 22:00
WEEKENDS: 6:00 TO 21:00

38:27.972 --> 38:30.266
- Hi.
- Hi.

38:30.349 --> 38:31.976
What is that? A battle request?

38:39.900 --> 38:41.110
I guess you don't know it.

38:44.030 --> 38:45.656
I ENJOYED THE RICE CAKE, THANK YOU

38:45.740 --> 38:48.200
You're such a good girl. Thank you.

38:49.410 --> 38:50.953
You know they offer deliveries, right?

38:51.037 --> 38:53.456
- Yes, Myungwon Rice Cake Shop.
- Yes.

38:54.040 --> 38:57.126
If you want rice cakes later,
ask your family to buy them from there.

38:58.544 --> 39:02.089
By the way,
are you really a police officer?

39:02.173 --> 39:03.841
Of course I am.

39:06.093 --> 39:07.345
Look.

39:08.929 --> 39:10.723
It's even better than a police officer.

39:10.806 --> 39:14.018
When I get healthy,
I want to be just like you.

39:15.019 --> 39:17.480
- Are you sick right now?
- A little bit.

39:19.398 --> 39:23.944
When I was little, I was also really sick.
So I couldn't go to school for two years.

39:24.028 --> 39:25.613
- Really?
- Yes.

39:26.322 --> 39:27.990
But I'm totally fine and strong now.

39:28.074 --> 39:29.992
You will be even stronger than me,

39:30.785 --> 39:33.496
so you don't need to worry about anything.

39:34.747 --> 39:35.623
Thank you for this.

39:38.125 --> 39:39.668
Where are you going?

39:40.336 --> 39:41.253
To have a battle.

40:01.440 --> 40:02.400
How can I help you?

40:03.192 --> 40:05.820
I live downstairs, and it's been
so noisy since last night.

40:05.903 --> 40:07.780
Are you doing construction work in there?

40:07.863 --> 40:11.617
I'm sorry. I'm moving my furniture, so…

40:15.955 --> 40:17.540
In the middle of the night?

40:17.623 --> 40:19.792
I'm a person with initiative,

40:19.875 --> 40:21.836
so I have to do things when I decide to.

40:21.919 --> 40:23.003
I'm sorry.

40:23.087 --> 40:25.464
That's not initiative, it's an illness.

40:27.133 --> 40:28.592
It will never happen again.

40:29.885 --> 40:31.470
All right, then.

40:31.554 --> 40:34.014
We enjoyed the rice cake.

40:34.974 --> 40:36.600
How did you know it was me?

40:36.684 --> 40:39.019
- We never met before.
- I heard about you.

40:39.103 --> 40:41.397
Your daughter looks just like you,
she's lovely.

40:41.480 --> 40:42.940
You look lovely.

40:50.406 --> 40:52.241
Haven't you seen that man before?

40:52.324 --> 40:54.410
I got on the elevator
a few times with him,

40:54.493 --> 40:56.829
but it seems like
he's not interested in others.

40:57.955 --> 41:01.750
Both him and his wife are doctors,
but he doesn't work and just stays home.

41:02.460 --> 41:05.796
My mom said
they have a legal problem or something.

41:06.547 --> 41:08.716
Perhaps it's because
he just likes to be lazy.

41:08.799 --> 41:10.593
- Okay, then. Bye.
- What about you?

41:10.676 --> 41:12.720
Me? I'm going to work out.

41:17.725 --> 41:19.310
Goodbye.

41:24.732 --> 41:26.442
Are you home alone?

41:27.776 --> 41:29.528
My dad does parcel delivery work,

41:29.612 --> 41:31.989
and my mom helps with
sorting in the morning.

41:32.865 --> 41:33.782
What about school?

41:33.866 --> 41:35.743
I'm doing experience learning at home.

41:35.826 --> 41:40.080
These days, if we tell the school,
we can get 19 days of school off a year.

41:42.750 --> 41:43.918
Come with me.

41:45.753 --> 41:48.172
Let's do experience learning
of sports with me today.

41:52.885 --> 41:54.303
Oh, this is the place.

42:03.395 --> 42:04.438
Hi.

42:05.940 --> 42:06.774
This is nice.

42:10.486 --> 42:12.738
- Hi.
- Hi.

42:12.821 --> 42:15.616
I'm a resident here.
I heard I can come here anytime.

42:15.699 --> 42:17.576
Please wait.

42:17.660 --> 42:21.872
You can bring
your own sneakers and towels.

42:21.956 --> 42:24.917
But first, please write down
your building number and unit number.

42:27.962 --> 42:28.796
Hi.

42:29.588 --> 42:30.506
Hi.

42:31.090 --> 42:33.384
- Are you going to work out too?
- Yes.

42:33.467 --> 42:36.178
- Here.
- Thank you.

42:37.429 --> 42:39.598
YOON SAE-BOM - BUILDING 101, UNIT 501

42:41.892 --> 42:46.313
The public rental residents
are not allowed to enter.

42:47.773 --> 42:50.526
Why not? Is it because
of the maintenance fee?

42:50.609 --> 42:52.820
Well, the maintenance fee is one thing,

42:52.903 --> 42:54.780
but it's more because of the equipment.

42:54.863 --> 42:56.532
The regular residents paid for them,

42:56.615 --> 42:57.992
so some say that it's not fair

42:58.075 --> 43:00.828
if we let the public rental residents
use them freely.

43:02.496 --> 43:03.998
Okay, I'll work out at home.

43:04.665 --> 43:06.959
- Let's go.
- Ma'am.

43:08.168 --> 43:12.131
But if you get personal training from me,
I can help you with that.

43:12.214 --> 43:14.091
I'll work out at home.

43:18.762 --> 43:20.889
- Did you know?
- Yes.

43:21.640 --> 43:23.225
Then why didn't you tell me?

43:23.309 --> 43:25.519
I thought you'd be able to solve it.

43:25.603 --> 43:27.980
Is there anything else like
the Fire Prevention Act?

43:28.814 --> 43:30.899
When money is involved,
it's hard to solve it.

43:32.776 --> 43:34.236
But still, there is a way.

43:34.820 --> 43:36.530
- One.
- One.

43:37.156 --> 43:38.365
- Two.
- Two.

43:39.158 --> 43:40.409
- Three.
- Three.

43:40.492 --> 43:41.910
Slowly.

43:41.994 --> 43:44.330
- Four.
- Four.

43:44.413 --> 43:45.706
You're good.

43:45.789 --> 43:47.666
- Five.
- Five.

43:47.750 --> 43:49.251
Let's go do that one over there.

43:57.885 --> 43:59.762
What do you learn in PE class these days?

43:59.845 --> 44:02.306
- Running.
- Oh, are you a good runner?

44:02.389 --> 44:03.223
No.

44:03.849 --> 44:05.351
I'm totally good at running.

44:29.708 --> 44:31.627
WIFE

44:37.383 --> 44:38.926
MISSED CALL: WIFE

45:12.042 --> 45:14.002
Since you worked out, get some good rest.

45:15.045 --> 45:16.588
Goodbye.

45:21.635 --> 45:22.469
She's cute.

45:26.807 --> 45:27.808
Hey.

45:27.891 --> 45:31.145
Sae-bom, help me.

45:32.146 --> 45:35.941
I got scratched by that trainee.

45:37.776 --> 45:40.195
I was too scared to say it, but…

45:40.863 --> 45:42.489
the wound isn't healing.

45:42.990 --> 45:44.283
Where are you?

45:45.117 --> 45:46.118
I'll be right there.

45:55.377 --> 45:56.336
It'll be okay.

45:57.087 --> 45:58.547
Look at me. I'm okay.

45:59.298 --> 46:00.549
You just need to get tested

46:01.258 --> 46:03.469
and get some rest today.
You'll be fine after.

46:05.596 --> 46:07.931
I'll tell your wife that
you're not cheating on her.

46:10.434 --> 46:13.854
I'm scared to think that I'm going to die.

46:13.937 --> 46:15.397
You won't die!

46:15.981 --> 46:17.191
You didn't get bitten.

46:17.774 --> 46:18.609
Look at me.

46:20.110 --> 46:21.278
It really is nothing.

46:22.613 --> 46:25.949
You just need to get tested
and confirm things today.

46:27.034 --> 46:28.994
I'll ask them to give you
additional points.

46:38.587 --> 46:40.672
You're not thirsty, are you?

46:44.718 --> 46:48.889
STOP

46:55.062 --> 46:56.813
There's one more patient.

47:17.292 --> 47:18.835
Let me see the wound.

47:36.144 --> 47:37.771
Are you sure it was a scratch?

47:39.189 --> 47:42.067
It looks like it was cut with a blade,
done quite recently.

47:44.236 --> 47:45.904
I wish that were the case.

47:48.031 --> 47:49.866
My wound isn't healing properly, either.

47:53.495 --> 47:55.664
It doesn't seem that serious
from how it looks.

47:56.790 --> 47:58.292
Let's test it.

48:03.297 --> 48:05.591
- What is different when it's serious?
- The color.

48:06.592 --> 48:08.885
The color turns dark red,
starting from the wound.

48:15.517 --> 48:17.269
Stay here until the test is over.

48:20.731 --> 48:22.441
Aren't you going to uncuff me?

48:39.666 --> 48:41.835
This is enough space
for you to move, right?

48:43.920 --> 48:45.130
Tell me if you're thirsty.

48:46.214 --> 48:48.008
Ms. Yoon, come out for a moment.

48:53.722 --> 48:54.848
See? I told you.

48:55.641 --> 48:56.642
It's okay.

48:57.434 --> 48:59.311
I'll go have my blood drawn. Wait here.

49:17.287 --> 49:18.455
It's okay.

49:20.082 --> 49:21.500
Nothing will happen.

49:22.918 --> 49:24.628
I'm just going to make money and go.

49:26.296 --> 49:27.422
It's okay.

49:54.157 --> 49:56.827
When something like this happens again,
tell us beforehand.

49:57.619 --> 49:59.329
I don't want to get startled.

50:01.289 --> 50:04.334
I got it. So can you please open the bag?

50:12.259 --> 50:15.220
MYUNGWON RICE CAKE SHOP

50:20.767 --> 50:23.395
They say you should spoil
the people you dislike.

50:40.495 --> 50:41.913
About the trainee…

50:42.914 --> 50:44.708
The one who got bitten by Lee Jong-tae.

50:46.501 --> 50:47.919
I heard he's in bad condition.

50:48.712 --> 50:50.881
Even his family's request to visit
got rejected.

50:59.556 --> 51:02.684
When they're bitten,
they get infected, no matter what.

51:04.519 --> 51:08.231
The condition worsens,
so less time is spent being normal.

51:09.441 --> 51:12.194
We never know when he'll feel thirsty
and attack someone,

51:12.277 --> 51:14.446
so it's impossible for him
to meet any visitors.

51:16.531 --> 51:17.616
What about the cure?

51:20.911 --> 51:22.245
There's none at this point.

51:23.830 --> 51:26.458
Once it gets worse,
they feel thirsty all the time.

51:26.541 --> 51:28.877
They lose their minds
and attack anyone they see.

51:30.545 --> 51:32.005
What we can do now

51:32.088 --> 51:34.466
is to slow down the speed
of reaching that condition.

51:38.512 --> 51:41.431
So it's true that no one
got out of here alive.

51:45.435 --> 51:48.772
You're an extremely lucky case.

51:50.941 --> 51:54.069
If nothing goes wrong, I'm sure
Mr. Lee Seung-young will be the same.

52:05.247 --> 52:07.415
Are you bored? Want something to eat?

52:24.933 --> 52:26.059
Where are you right now?

52:30.105 --> 52:31.189
I have a family.

52:32.816 --> 52:36.027
If I die for nothing, they'll keep
the reason for my death secret.

52:36.111 --> 52:37.529
Sae-bom.

52:37.612 --> 52:40.866
There's a way to make money,
and safety is guaranteed.

52:40.949 --> 52:43.159
Hello? Seung-young!

52:58.174 --> 53:01.636
The call cannot be connected.
Please leave a message…

53:01.720 --> 53:03.430
Is this really okay?

53:03.513 --> 53:05.515
What if everyone is dying in there?

53:05.599 --> 53:07.350
I got a call from a journalist.

53:07.434 --> 53:10.937
He said he'll pay me
if I tell him what happened here.

53:29.539 --> 53:33.335
He put on a biohazard suit and escaped.
They thought he was bringing out chairs.

53:33.418 --> 53:35.545
Where are the seriously ill patients?

53:37.464 --> 53:38.590
Where are they?

53:40.383 --> 53:43.553
We put them in a freezer storage
for food in the basement,

53:43.637 --> 53:46.473
but they increased in number,
so we had to move them elsewhere.

53:46.556 --> 53:48.391
So, where is this "elsewhere?"

53:50.685 --> 53:51.645
A freezer truck.

56:40.563 --> 56:41.940
Damn it.

56:57.330 --> 56:58.331
DAMN JOURNALIST

56:58.414 --> 57:01.042
DID YOU THINK ABOUT OUR OFFER?

57:04.504 --> 57:06.005
DAMN JOURNALIST

57:10.969 --> 57:12.428
You should pay me first.

57:12.512 --> 57:15.849
If you do,
I'll send you the footage right away.

57:17.142 --> 57:21.438
This call is being recorded,
so don't think about tricking me later.

57:23.898 --> 57:25.984
Pay me half of it first, at least!

57:32.740 --> 57:34.451
Send the money and call me.

57:34.993 --> 57:35.827
This…

57:37.120 --> 57:38.663
is a huge story.

58:19.746 --> 58:21.789
SEYANG DREAM CAR WASH

58:24.501 --> 58:26.336
They're in there. Why aren't you going?

58:26.419 --> 58:28.671
Someone's supposed to come here.

58:28.755 --> 58:30.381
Who? Did you ask for backup?

58:31.174 --> 58:32.383
There he is.

58:34.344 --> 58:35.428
What?

58:36.054 --> 58:39.182
Hello, Lieutenant Colonel Han Tae-seok.

58:39.265 --> 58:40.975
What brings you to this shabby place?

58:41.059 --> 58:44.812
I'd like to meet the dealer
with Corporal Jung only. Is that okay?

58:45.772 --> 58:49.442
Sure, that's fine.
I can just wait here, then.

58:56.449 --> 58:57.909
- Hey! You…
- I know.

58:57.992 --> 58:59.369
Stay here.

59:01.329 --> 59:03.039
I hate him, seriously…

59:03.623 --> 59:05.542
By the way, why are you really here?

59:06.125 --> 59:08.711
The remaining Next was kept
in the company's storage.

59:08.795 --> 59:10.880
I want to find out
who spread it in the market.

59:10.964 --> 59:14.717
It seems like this infectious disease
is making a mess overseas too.

59:14.801 --> 59:16.761
Has Next been sold worldwide?

59:17.387 --> 59:21.683
I told you I'm not good at making things,
but I'm good at stealing things, right?

59:23.059 --> 59:25.228
It's a foreign drug.
I stole it while I was

59:25.311 --> 59:27.230
in the Competitiveness Reinforcement Team.

59:30.483 --> 59:31.693
You are an incredible man.

59:47.584 --> 59:48.543
Total of three.

59:49.419 --> 59:50.795
Damn it, turn the light off!

59:56.926 --> 59:58.595
You brought the money, right?

59:59.929 --> 01:00:01.598
Where is Lee Jong-tae?

01:00:05.935 --> 01:00:08.062
That jerk Lee Jong-tae…

01:00:08.146 --> 01:00:09.731
I bet you can't reach him.

01:00:22.493 --> 01:00:25.288
- There are two of them.
- There are three of them.

01:00:33.963 --> 01:00:34.881
The drug.

01:00:36.924 --> 01:00:38.009
In the trunk…

01:00:38.092 --> 01:00:39.552
Cuff them while I get them.

01:00:52.982 --> 01:00:54.692
You assholes! You're all dead now!

01:01:16.381 --> 01:01:17.256
What is this?

01:01:18.966 --> 01:01:20.551
A Glock. You've never seen one?

01:01:20.635 --> 01:01:22.804
I mean, why are you carrying that around?

01:01:31.312 --> 01:01:33.106
What do you think you're doing?

01:01:33.189 --> 01:01:34.982
Making sure it's dead.

01:01:36.609 --> 01:01:38.736
You dare to kill a person
in front of a cop?

01:01:39.904 --> 01:01:41.823
Do you think this is a human being?

01:01:57.004 --> 01:01:58.589
All of you, hands up!

01:01:59.257 --> 01:02:00.299
Hands up…

01:02:01.384 --> 01:02:02.927
It's all done.

01:02:03.594 --> 01:02:05.513
Oh, really? Gosh.

01:02:06.097 --> 01:02:09.142
Hey! How many shots did you fire?

01:02:09.225 --> 01:02:12.353
If this was a residential area,
you'd get disciplined again!

01:02:13.938 --> 01:02:15.022
Did you do all this?

01:02:31.664 --> 01:02:34.208
Since when has that thing
been in that condition?

01:02:34.292 --> 01:02:35.334
I don't know.

01:02:37.920 --> 01:02:41.507
I just went to his house
to get paid, and he was like that.

01:02:41.591 --> 01:02:43.509
He bit his whole family and killed them.

01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:46.637
He was banging his head
on the puddle of blood!

01:02:47.764 --> 01:02:50.308
- Did it take Next?
- Tons of it.

01:02:50.391 --> 01:02:52.602
He's been like that the whole time.

01:02:52.685 --> 01:02:54.687
And you did that to someone ill?

01:02:56.773 --> 01:02:58.357
What else would I have done?

01:02:58.941 --> 01:03:01.778
He was the best guard dog ever.
I didn't even have to feed him.

01:03:06.699 --> 01:03:08.785
All of you took that drug, right?

01:03:08.868 --> 01:03:10.703
You'll become like that soon.

01:03:14.248 --> 01:03:15.792
- Get up, you jerk.
- Hello?

01:03:18.127 --> 01:03:18.961
Okay.

01:03:19.712 --> 01:03:23.424
Mr. Jung, we have a problem at the dorm.

01:03:23.508 --> 01:03:24.342
So?

01:03:25.092 --> 01:03:26.302
Ms. Yoon Sae-bom is there.

01:03:29.055 --> 01:03:30.765
Why did she go there again?

01:03:52.870 --> 01:03:54.372
They're not humans.

01:03:56.415 --> 01:03:57.583
What do you mean?

01:03:58.751 --> 01:03:59.710
None of them are.

01:04:22.567 --> 01:04:23.609
Quiet!

01:04:30.449 --> 01:04:31.325
Open this.

01:04:32.243 --> 01:04:33.286
Now!

01:04:36.706 --> 01:04:38.165
No, don't open it!

01:05:53.449 --> 01:05:54.283
Be honest.

01:05:55.952 --> 01:05:57.912
You're seeing those people as monsters.

01:05:58.746 --> 01:05:59.789
They told us to stop.

01:05:59.872 --> 01:06:02.792
Mad Human Disease is spreading
in the apartment.

01:06:02.875 --> 01:06:05.378
Those drugs cause
Mad Human Disease, right?

01:06:06.170 --> 01:06:08.923
Bad rumors don't help with house prices.

01:06:09.006 --> 01:06:10.132
We're stopping them all.

01:06:10.216 --> 01:06:12.551
So you lock them up
and wait until they die?

01:06:12.635 --> 01:06:15.763
I'm sure there's something
about that woman upstairs.

01:06:16.514 --> 01:06:19.433
What's going on in that house right now?

01:06:22.728 --> 01:06:27.733
Subtitle translation by: Hae-lim Lee
